                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "140a22b5-18b2-317d-92f1-2a375e2364b1",
                        "entry_id": "dd9e23f6-e235-3a50-8c12-2347b0bf275e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Troubled, confused."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "167e2dc3-d2e6-4e85-a3c9-ee4df2f58dce",
                                "sense_id": "140a22b5-18b2-317d-92f1-2a375e2364b1",
                                "text": "On thother side they saw the warlike Mayd / Al in her snow-white smocke, with locks unbowned, / Threatning the point of her avenging blaed; / That with so troublous terror they were all dismayd."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "11eb8dc0-6a3f-46e6-8cf8-8ea7d4ffefe5",
                                "sense_id": "140a22b5-18b2-317d-92f1-2a375e2364b1",
                                "text": "The troublous Day has brawled itself to rest: no lives yet lost but that of one warhorse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "15238c4a-e01a-494f-ba36-68dd314f2885",
                                "sense_id": "140a22b5-18b2-317d-92f1-2a375e2364b1",
                                "text": "By and by he fell into a troublous sleep—it seemed that he was going to be stoned, and then he was in battle, and then shipwrecked in the water–[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dcf3d1fc-41d5-3b88-badc-47659d5a1ec3",
                        "entry_id": "dd9e23f6-e235-3a50-8c12-2347b0bf275e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Causing trouble; troublesome, vexatious."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ec6056b-d0e2-4a47-892f-991594fc5d4d",
                                "sense_id": "dcf3d1fc-41d5-3b88-badc-47659d5a1ec3",
                                "text": "the mystery, the pervasive melancholy, the vaguely troublous forecast and retrospect which possess the mind in contemplating this sequestered spot, unhallowed save by the sense of a common humanity [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9122a131-018e-4b6c-b723-96f2fd55efb7",
                                "sense_id": "dcf3d1fc-41d5-3b88-badc-47659d5a1ec3",
                                "text": "The whole waited, for didn't there hang behind this troublous foreground the vast vagueness which the English themselves spoke of as \"abroad\"?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
